From 4e6746c131560c78097b41d97b5c0d5dcb2988c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:28:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: j716s: Build in the MTP haptic driver

HID_MAGICMOUSE, which drives the trackpad, depends on
HID_APPLE_MTP_HAPTIC || !HID_APPLE_MTP_HAPTIC, and asahi.config has the
haptic driver as =m, so with it left alone magicmouse would be capped at
=m. The J716s root has no modules, so this fragment forced the haptic
driver off. =y satisfies the same dependency, so build both in.

The haptic driver binds to the trackpad's actuator HID device (the
"actuator" node of the MTP DockChannel, already in t6050-j716s.dts), puts
it in device-controlled mode, and gives hid-magicmouse the host haptics
interface. The click strength stays with the firmware: no
apple,click-strength is set for this board.

With defconfig, asahi.config and j716s.config both are =y, and
hid-apple-mtp-haptic.o and hid-magicmouse.o build. Booted on the J716s
(alone, and with the netfilter and kernel crypto fragments): two
haptic input devices register.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config b/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
index 83f1eca906e5..3e9078f72154 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
@@ -26,13 +26,14 @@ CONFIG_ARM_APPLE_SOC_CPUFREQ=y
 CONFIG_PINCTRL_APPLE_GPIO=y
 
 # Keyboard and trackpad: DockChannel HID. HID_MAGICMOUSE drives the
-# trackpad; the MTP haptic driver would force it to =m, so it stays off
-# (no click haptics).
+# trackpad and depends on HID_APPLE_MTP_HAPTIC || !HID_APPLE_MTP_HAPTIC, so
+# the MTP haptic driver (the trackpad's click actuator) is built in with it:
+# asahi.config has the haptic driver as =m, which would cap magicmouse at =m.
 CONFIG_APPLE_DOCKCHANNEL=y
 CONFIG_HID_DOCKCHANNEL=y
 CONFIG_HID_APPLE=y
+CONFIG_HID_APPLE_MTP_HAPTIC=y
 CONFIG_HID_MAGICMOUSE=y
-CONFIG_HID_APPLE_MTP_HAPTIC=n
 CONFIG_HIDRAW=y
 
 # Keyboard backlight and the backlight class
